  "title": "Bus & train",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**থেকে** 'from' pairs with **পর্যন্ত** (*porjonto*) 'to, as far as': **ঢাকা থেকে সিলেট পর্যন্ত** 'from Dhaka to Sylhet'. Don't confuse it with **দিয়ে** 'via, along'.\n\nThe future of 'go' by person:\n\n- **যাব** — আমি, আমরা\n- **যাবে** — তুমি, সে, and things like a bus or a train\n- **যাবেন** — আপনি, তিনি\n\nSo **এই বাস কি ঢাকা যাবে?** 'Does this bus go to Dhaka?' (lit. 'will this bus go…'). The yes/no **কি** sits right after the subject.\n\n'By bus / by train' takes the locative: **বাসে**, **ট্রেনে**. Watch the ending — **বাসে** (*base*) 'by bus' is not **বাসায়** (*bashay*) 'at home'.\n\nBuying a ticket is simply **একটা টিকিট দেন** 'One ticket, please' — **দুইটা টিকিট দেন** for two.\n\n**Culture:** on Dhaka's local buses a helper hangs at the door calling out the stops. Listen for place names and check with **এই বাস কি … যাবে?** before you board. Intercity trains leave (**ছাড়বে**, 'will leave') from Kamalapur and Airport stations; buy your **টিকিট** well before Eid, when everyone travels home.",
